Binding rules (from the plan, §1):
- Implementers and verifiers: Agent tool, subagent_type "general-purpose", model "sonnet".
  Verifier is never the same agent as the implementer. Re-rounds go back to the SAME
  implementer via SendMessage (max 2), then re-brief a fresh one.
- TDD: implementer writes tests first, pastes RED output, implements, pastes GREEN.
  No RED evidence = reject without review.
- Verifier: checks git status for out-of-scope edits, reruns the task's tests, writes >=3
  NEW adversarial tests (edge list + own ideas), keeps passing ones in the suite,
  verdict PASS/FAIL with repro.
- Token budget per agent: close at 100-150k; at 100k and not done -> stop and report.
  Briefs must be self-contained (decision table rows, exact symbols, line ranges from a
  fresh grep, do-not-read list, exact commands) so agents never explore.
- Parallelism: Phase 1 sequential (T1->V1->T2->V2). Phase 2 = T3,T4,T5,T6 in parallel,
  each with its own verifier; disjoint files; NO full-suite runs in Phase 2. Phase 3 =
  T7 and T8 in parallel. Then the Gate (§3). Launch parallel agents in ONE message.
- R binary is "/c/Program Files/R/R-4.5.3/bin/x64/Rscript" (full path, quoted). Bare
  Rscript is R 4.6.1 with an empty library. Never use the MCP R session.
- Tests must never spawn background processes or file-lock helpers (antivirus). Mock seams.
- test-live.R: edit by reading only, never run.
- Never hand-edit man/ or NAMESPACE; roxygen then roxygen2::roxygenise(). Examples and
  tests must never write to the real user cache dir.
- Commits: orchestrator only, conventional prefixes, NO co-author trailer.
  Do not commit tools/working-on-raw-sync-locked-files.md (belongs to another branch).

Start now with Phase 0 leftovers: write briefs T1-T8 into tools/briefs/ using the §4
